00:18:52,063 --> 00:18:54,766
WOMAN: Does Dennis Rodman know more about Kim Jong-Un at this point?

214
00:18:54,866 --> 00:18:57,469
than any American? MAN: He is that man.

215
00:18:57,569 --> 00:19:02,274
There's no one in the CIA who can tell you more about Kim Jong-Un than Dennis Rodman.

216
00:19:02,374 --> 00:19:03,475
And that is worrying.

217
00:19:05,043 --> 00:19:08,647
RODMAN: Happy birthday to you.

218
00:19:08,747 --> 00:19:13,117
Happy birthday to you.

219
00:19:13,218 --> 00:19:17,456
Happy birthday dear officer.

220
00:19:17,556 --> 00:19:20,958
Happy birthday to you.

221
00:19:21,059 --> 00:19:23,162
(apalusos)

222
00:19:27,765 --> 00:19:32,905
NARRATOR: Rodman's visit to Pyongyang fulfilled a childhood dream for Kim Jong-Un.

223
00:19:38,110 --> 00:19:42,080
But being an all-powerful dictator of the most secretive state on Earth

224
00:19:42,180 --> 00:19:43,882
is not without challenges.

225
00:19:46,852 --> 00:19:51,723
The generals at the heart of the regime were trying to outdo the young Kim,

226
00:19:51,823 --> 00:19:54,593
in an effort to overthrow the inexperienced leader.

227
00:19:57,328 --> 00:20:01,266
But Kim Jong-Un was about to prove that he was just as ruthless.

228
00:20:01,366 --> 00:20:03,402
as the past Kims had been.

229
00:20:18,516 --> 00:20:28,693
(music)

230
00:20:28,793 --> 00:20:31,463
NARRATOR: Kim Jong-Un is a 21st-century dictator.

231
00:20:35,833 --> 00:20:40,038
I was happy to accept certain kinds of progress,

232
00:20:40,138 --> 00:20:44,442
but maintaining complete control is essential,

233
00:20:44,543 --> 00:20:47,646
as well as the loyalty of its inner sanctuary.

234
00:20:50,415 --> 00:20:54,519
READ: One of the things I asked for when I worked as a journalist in North Korea,

235
00:20:54,619 --> 00:20:58,457
was that I was allowed to attend a private meeting.

236
00:20:59,257 --> 00:21:02,260
